cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these signatures or the methodology, please cite this work."
title: "ai-agent-attack-signatures: Traffic Signatures and Detection Methodology for AI-Powered Penetration-Testing Agents"
abstract: >-
  An empirical study of 65 AI pentest frameworks that determines which ones leave an
  attributable fingerprint on the target side. Ships 272 validated strong signatures
  (zero hits across 9.9M public internet requests and 142,705 real WAF attack
  transactions), a behavioural detector reaching 86.7% segment recall at a 2.72%
  false-positive rate on 1,582 real attackers, and a measured account of where
  attribution provably fails.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/<owner>/ai-agent-attack-signatures"
keywords:
  - security
  - ai-agents
  - penetration-testing
  - detection
  - network-traffic
  - threat-detection
  - ioc
